{"name":"Nana’s Rose","hex":"#de9eaa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nana","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A banana.","A foolish person."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One's grandmother.","A nanny."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nana"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nana (entertainer)","blocks":[{"text":"Im Jin-ah, known professionally as Nana (나나), is a South Korean singer, actress, and model. She first rose to prominence as a former member of the South Korean girl group After School and its subgroups, Orange Caramel and After School Red. As an actress, Nana has starred in various television dramas such as Love Weaves Through a Millennium (2015), The Good Wife (2016), Kill It (2019), and Justice (2019)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Nana_in_September_2026.png/330px-Nana_in_September_2026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nana_(entertainer)","wikidata":"Q491515"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose","wikidata":"Q34687"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)","wikidata":"Q533047"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Nana_in_2011_Seoul_Fashion_Week.jpg/500px-Nana_in_2011_Seoul_Fashion_Week.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Nana_in_2011_Seoul_Fashion_Week.jpg/1280px-Nana_in_2011_Seoul_Fashion_Week.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Nana_in_2011_Seoul_Fashion_Week.jpg/500px-Nana_in_2011_Seoul_Fashion_Week.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nana at the 2011 Seoul Fashion Week","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANana_in_2011_Seoul_Fashion_Week.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/150802_%EC%98%A4%EB%A0%8C%EC%A7%80%EC%BA%AC%EB%9D%BC%EB%A9%9C_22.jpg/500px-150802_%EC%98%A4%EB%A0%8C%EC%A7%80%EC%BA%AC%EB%9D%BC%EB%A9%9C_22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/150802_%EC%98%A4%EB%A0%8C%EC%A7%80%EC%BA%AC%EB%9D%BC%EB%A9%9C_22.jpg/1280px-150802_%EC%98%A4%EB%A0%8C%EC%A7%80%EC%BA%AC%EB%9D%BC%EB%A9%9C_22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/15